# $project

An interactive machine learning practice built on
[mpc-iml-toolkit](https://github.com/BenTsai0212/mpc-iml-toolkit) v$version. The
toolkit is a dependency pinned to a git tag in `pyproject.toml`; this repository
contains none of its code.

If the tag `v$version` does not exist yet, point the dependency at a local checkout
of the toolkit instead: `uv add --editable <path to mpc-iml-toolkit>`.

## Install

```bash
uv sync
```

## Record

With the MPC Sample connected over USB:

```bash
uv run python -m mpc_iml.record examples.jsonl --duration 10
```

Mark examples with `example_start` / `example_end` lines (ADR 0002 of the toolkit);
`tests/data/example.jsonl` is a small hand-written example.

## Run

Train on a recording and run on a replay (the second file defaults to the first):

```bash
uv run python -m $package tests/data/example.jsonl
```

Add `--osc` to send `/wek/inputs` and `/wek/outputs` with Wekinator's default ports.

## Where to edit

- `src/$package/model.py`: your model (`fit` and `predict`, the toolkit's
  `mpc_iml.model.Model`). It starts empty and always predicts `[0.0]`.
- `src/$package/__main__.py`: how examples are loaded and the loop is run.

## Checks

```bash
uv run ruff check
uv run ruff format --check
uv run mypy
uv run pytest
```
